  "document_contents": {
    "comment.41696": "Our lawmakers were travelling with taxpayer monies decades ago to review rail systems in the states and abroad.  Unfortunately most of them as with our lawmakers today have little to no experience with actually using these systems. We were fortunate to have Frank Fasi as Mayor for many years. \"The Bus\" system we have today is his legacy.  Prior to that we had the HRT, Hawaii's plantation era's green meat wagons. Lack of experience fuels lack of vision.",
    "comment.41719": "I suppose if they're looking for footprints having others making them is counter-productive, but isn't that an even greater case for using drones?",
    "comment.55617": "StanleyJ: The \"battle\" over legalization of marijuana is over. I think the real issues today involve just how the industry is going to \"fit into\" communities. When individuals move into a small community such as Creswell and, essentially, strive to \"redefine\" that community.....\"make it the Pot Cupertino\", becoming to the marijuana industry what Cupertino, California was to the dot.com era, they shouldn't be surprised when there is  some opposition.\n\nDan Issacson, described as \"the face\" of One Grow, promises Creswell \"wealth and fame\", as the Pot Capital of Oregon and open embraces the \"dot.com\" business plan. For those who may not remember, the \"dot.com\" business plan involved building a business which \"looked\" great, promoting it successfully, then \"taking it public\" and pocketing the profits from the sale, leaving the new shareholders with a worthless company. ....Hence, the concept of the \"dot.com\" bust. IMO, One Grow's openly boasting of a \"dot.com\" approach (cont)",
    "comment.69522": "Sweden and Germany, just to give two examples, which have no immigration limits and refuse to set any.  And just look at all the social upheaval and economic costs that heavy migration into those nations in recent years, along with the inability and/or unwillingness of many of those migrants to assimilate or adapt to the prevailing culture, has resulted in.\n\nI am not anti-immigrant, but there is a distinction between controlled immigration and wholesale and unlimited migration.  The historical record is clear on the detrimental and often disastrous results of the latter."
  }
